# W7: GIFs and pictures from other sites in the real app (WM), against the showcase scenario, as
# alexk in Couch Co-op's #general. The fake server's own /__fixtures/ stands in for the GIF
# service's media host and for a link preview's site; every fetch from it is a Fixture_image request,
# so "nothing was asked" is a count.
# - No GIF service: no GIF button. With one: the button.
# - "Load images from other sites" off: the picker offers Allow and nothing is fetched; Allow turns
#   the one switch on, the featured grid loads and its previews are fetched.
# - Search, load more, Escape; a pick sends the GIF's URL as the message: the list shows the GIF,
#   and after a restart (read again from the server) it still does.
# - The switch off in Settings: the same message is a "GIF from 127.0.0.1: Load" card and nothing is
#   fetched; Load turns it on again. A link preview's picture: off, then on, without a restart.

app 1280 800
window activate
wait idle
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username" within 5
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core connection connected
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core rows >= 14
wait idle

# 1. The server has no GIF service: no button.
wait core no-element composer-gif
shot 01-no-gif-button

# 2. It has one: after a restart (the server's settings are read again), the button.
server public_settings "{\"gifSearchEnabled\": true}"
restart
wait core session signed-in
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core element composer-gif within 10
wait core w7 third-party off
wait idle
shot 02-gif-button

# 3. The picker while third-party pictures are off: the Allow notice, and nothing fetched.
w7 mark
click composer-gif
wait core w7 picker open
wait core w7 picker notice
wait idle
shot 03-picker-allow
expect core w7 new-requests Fixture_image == 0
expect core w7 new-requests GifsController_featured == 0

# 4. Allow: the one switch goes on (core and the settings store), the featured grid loads and its
# previews are fetched.
click gif-allow
wait core w7 third-party on
expect settings /third_party_media true
wait core w7 picker results >= 20 within 10
wait core w7 new-requests Fixture_image >= 1 within 10
wait idle
shot 04-featured

# 5. Search: after Allow the caret is in the search field again; the picker waits out its
# debounce (the rig's clock moves by `tick`), then core reads the query.
type "Fixture GIF 2"
tick 300
wait core w7 picker query "Fixture GIF 2" within 5
wait core w7 picker results >= 11 within 10
wait idle
shot 05-search

# 6. The featured list again, and its next page.
click gif-search-clear
tick 300
wait core w7 picker query "" within 5
wait core w7 picker results >= 20 within 10
click gif-more
wait core w7 picker results >= 30 within 10
expect requests GifsController_featured >= 2

# 7. Its close button closes it; opened again, Escape does, and the typing goes back to the
# composer.
click gif-close
wait core w7 picker closed
click composer-gif
wait core w7 picker open
press escape
wait core w7 picker closed
type "x"
wait core composer-text "x"
press backspace

# 8. Open again and pick the third GIF: its URL alone is the message, and the list draws the GIF.
click composer-gif
wait core w7 picker results >= 20 within 10
click gif-gif-3
wait core w7 picker closed
wait core w7 sent-gif "/__fixtures/gif-3.gif" within 10
wait core requests sendMessage >= 1
wait core w7 gif shown within 10
wait idle
shot 08-sent

# 9. Read again from the server after a restart: still the GIF.
link-images on
restart
wait core session signed-in
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core w7 sent-gif "/__fixtures/gif-3.gif" within 10
wait core w7 gif shown within 10
wait idle
shot 09-sent-reloaded

# 10. The switch off in Settings: the GIF is a Load card, and nothing is fetched.
click rail-account
wait core label "Settings"
click account-settings
wait core route settings/notifications
click settings-tab-desktop
wait core route settings/desktop
click desktop-link-preview-images
wait core w7 third-party off
expect settings /third_party_media false
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
w7 mark
wait core w7 gif blocked within 10
expect label "GIF from 127.0.0.1"
wait idle
shot 10-blocked
expect core w7 new-requests Fixture_image == 0

# 11. Load: on again for everything, and the GIF is fetched and drawn.
w7 click-gif-load
wait core w7 third-party on
expect settings /third_party_media true
wait core w7 gif shown within 10
wait idle
shot 11-loaded

# 12. A link preview's picture, at runtime: drawn while on; off, a Load card and no request; on, drawn
# again (fetched afresh: turning off dropped what was kept).
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"a picture elsewhere \", \"linkPreview\": {\"url\": \"https://example.invalid/w7\", \"title\": \"A W7 article\", \"description\": \"Its picture is on another site.\", \"siteName\": \"Example\", \"imageUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1:3999/__fixtures/w7-preview.png\"}}"
wait core text "a picture elsewhere"
w7 mark
click rail-account
wait core label "Settings"
click account-settings
wait core route settings/notifications
click settings-tab-desktop
wait core route settings/desktop
click desktop-link-preview-images
wait core w7 third-party off
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core text "a picture elsewhere"
expect label "Image from 127.0.0.1"
wait idle
shot 12-preview-off
expect core w7 new-requests Fixture_image == 0
click rail-account
wait core label "Settings"
click account-settings
wait core route settings/notifications
click settings-tab-desktop
wait core route settings/desktop
click desktop-link-preview-images
wait core w7 third-party on
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core w7 new-requests Fixture_image >= 2 within 10
wait idle
shot 13-preview-on

# 14. At phone width the composer's "+" sheet offers GIF, and the picker is a bottom sheet.
app 390 844
wait core session signed-in
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
click composer-actions
wait core element composer-gif
click composer-gif
wait core w7 picker open
wait core w7 picker results >= 20 within 10
wait idle
shot 14-phone-sheet
